<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
      THIS COMMENT IS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT ON PURPOSE - a comment ABOVE the root breaks sf
      at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml" error.

      MASTER-DETAIL to Checklist__c, for the same reasons recorded on Checklist__c: the grandparent
      Transaction__c is sharingModel=Private, these rows are machine-created by a Queueable, and a
      Private-OWD lookup child would be OWNED by the automation user and invisible to the deal team
      until sharing rules were written. The chain Transaction__c to Checklist__c to Checklist_Item__c
      makes access identical to access on the deal, with nothing to maintain and nothing to drift.

      NO OwnerId. Owner_Label__c is a ROLE STRING; Completed_By__c is the real person. Do not pair
      Owner_Label__c with a completion date and render it as "completed by role" - TaskSelector and
      TransactionTaskController both carry warnings that this reads as a lie.

      FLAG__c IS A SINGLE LOSSY PICKLIST, BY EXPLICIT USER DECISION (GATE-B6), against the design
      recommendation to split it. Completing a CRITICAL item OVERWRITES the CRITICAL severity with
      Completed or Verified, so "show me all critical items" can only ever return OPEN ones and
      "how many critical items did this deal have" is unanswerable from Flag__c. That loss is known
      and accepted.

      THAT IS WHY TWO SEPARATE IMMUTABLE MARKERS EXIST AND ARE MANDATORY, NOT OPTIONAL:
        Is_Critical__c          - the severity. Seeded from the definition on B2, F12, I7 and J4 and
                                  never overwritten by working the item. Reports group on THIS,
                                  never on Flag__c.
        Is_Wire_Verification__c - seeded on B2 and I7. This is what Transaction__c.Wire_Open_Risks__c
                                  counts after cutover. It REPLACES the
                                  Subject.toLowerCase().contains('anti-fraud') string parse in
                                  TaskRollupService, which reads ZERO silently, with no error
                                  anywhere, the moment the subject text changes.
      Wire_Open_Risks__c CANNOT be derived from Flag__c. Do not try.

      DELETE IS NOT GRANTED to any persona permission set. Group-F removal on a Loan_Required__c
      true-to-false flip reconciles in system mode and refuses when any item in the group has been
      completed - deleting worked history is worse than an inconsistent checklist.

      🔴 CORRECTED 2026-08-31, POST-DEPLOY FAILURE - same fix and same reasoning as Checklist__c's
      own header note. enableSharing=false paired with enableBulkApi=true/enableStreamingApi=true
      is refused outright ("must be enabled together or disabled together"), regardless of
      sharingModel. Set to true to match Loan__c/Insurance_Binder__c. ControlledByParent still
      permits no sharing rules on this object either way.
    -->
    <allowInChatterGroups>false</allowInChatterGroups>
    <compactLayoutAssignment>SYSTEM</compactLayoutAssignment>
    <deploymentStatus>Deployed</deploymentStatus>
    <description>One line of the Transaction closing checklist. Master-detail child of Checklist__c and grandchild of Transaction__c, so access is inherited and there is no record owner. Replaces one Task record in the 82-Task model. Carries the wire-fraud verification evidence and the Blocked_By__c prerequisite link that gates a wire send behind its verbal verification.</description>
    <enableActivities>false</enableActivities>
    <enableBulkApi>true</enableBulkApi>
    <enableFeeds>false</enableFeeds>
    <enableHistory>false</enableHistory>
    <enableLicensing>false</enableLicensing>
    <enableReports>true</enableReports>
    <enableSearch>false</enableSearch>
    <enableSharing>true</enableSharing>
    <enableStreamingApi>true</enableStreamingApi>
    <externalSharingModel>ControlledByParent</externalSharingModel>
    <label>Checklist Item</label>
    <nameField>
        <displayFormat>CLI-{000000}</displayFormat>
        <label>Checklist Item Number</label>
        <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
        <type>AutoNumber</type>
    </nameField>
    <pluralLabel>Checklist Items</pluralLabel>
    <searchLayouts></searchLayouts>
    <sharingModel>ControlledByParent</sharingModel>
    <visibility>Public</visibility>
</CustomObject>
